# Shared Libraries (`pkg/lib`)

> Analyzed from commit: `baf9c7bcc307ed9358ad59886a5536366a050012` on 2026-09-17
> Source paths: `pkg/lib/`

## Package Purpose

`pkg/lib/` is the shared Go library forked from
[konveyor/controller v0.11.0](https://github.com/konveyor/controller/releases/tag/v0.11.0).
Every Forklift controller, inventory collector, and REST handler depends on these
packages for status conditions, inventory persistence, migration itineraries,
cross-resource reference tracking, structured logging, and error wrapping.
Understanding these patterns is prerequisite to reading any controller code.

---

## Key Types and Structs

### Condition (`pkg/lib/condition`)

```go
type Condition struct {
    Type               string   // e.g. "Ready", "ReconcileFailed"
    Status             string   // "True" or "False"
    Category           string   // Critical, Error, Warn, Required, Advisory, ...
    Reason             string
    Message            string
    Suggestion         string
    LastTransitionTime v1.Time
    Durable            bool     // survives staging sweeps
    Items              []string // referenced in Message
    staged             bool     // internal: set this reconcile cycle
}

type Conditions struct {
    List    []Condition
    staging bool
    explain Explain
}
```

Built-in types: `ReconcileFailed`, `Ready`. Built-in categories: `Critical`, `Error`,
`Warn`, `Required`, `Advisory`, plus pending-state categories `ValidatingVDDK`,
`VMMissingGuestIPs`, `VMMissingChangedBlockTracking`, `SharedDisks`.

### Itinerary (`pkg/lib/itinerary`)

```go
type Step struct {
