## Reconciliation / Execution Flow

### Condition staging (every controller)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[BeginStagingConditions] --> B[SetCondition / validation]
    B --> C[EndStagingConditions]
    C --> D[Derive Ready from HasBlockerCondition]
```

1. `BeginStagingConditions()` — marks all non-`Durable` conditions as un-staged
2. `SetCondition(...)` — adds/updates; marks `staged=true`
3. `EndStagingConditions()` — deletes un-staged conditions
4. Derive `Ready` from `!HasBlockerCondition()` (`Critical` or `Error` categories)

Controllers skip status patches when `Explain().Empty()` is true.

### Inventory collection

```
Provider reconciler → Container.Add(Collector) → Collector.Start()
  → goroutine syncs resources into SQLite via model.DB
  → REST API reads from DB via Collector.DB()
```

`Collection.Reconcile(desired)` performs delete stale → add new → update changed.

### Itinerary navigation (migration pipeline)

```
Itinerary.List()  → predicate-filtered steps
Itinerary.First() → first filtered step
Itinerary.Next(name) → (next Step, done bool, err)
Itinerary.Progress(step) → {Completed, Total}
```

### Reference-driven reconciliation

```
CR field tagged ref:"Kind" → EventMapper.Create/Update/Delete → RefMap
Referenced resource changes → ref.Handler(owner) → enqueue owner reconcile
```

